  "text": "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nElections - Scott County, Iowa\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n Scott County, Iowa\n \nElections\n \n \n\n \n\n \n \nVote\n \n \nRegister to Vote\n \nAbsentee (Early) Voting\n \nMaps\n \nMilitary/Overseas Voting\n \nPrecincts\n \nVoter ID\n \n \n \nElections\n \n \nUpcoming Elections\n \nPast Elections\n \nSample Ballots\n \nPoll Workers (Precinct Election Officials)\n \nTypes of Elections\n \n \n \nElected Officials\n \n \nFind Your Elected Officials\n \nFederal\n \nState\n \nCounty\n \nCity\n \nSchool Board\n \nTownship\n \n \n \nCandidates\n \nNews\n \nFAQ\n \nContact\n \nCounty Site\n \n Facebook\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n Click here to find an early voting location! \n\n\n\n\n \n\n \n\n \nWelcome to the Scott County Elections website.\n The Election Department in the Auditor’s Office is responsible for every aspect of conducting an election from voter registration to the final count of the votes. This site is designed to be a resource for residents looking to learn how to vote, find their elected officials, learn about becoming a candidate, or find past or upcoming election information.\n \n \n\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n \nQuick Links\n \nRegister to Vote\n \nWhere Do I Vote?\n \nEarly Voting Locations\n \nAm I Registered?\n \nHow Do I Vote?\n \nFind Your Elected Officials\n \n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n \nUpcoming & Recent Elections\n \n\n \n\n \nNov\n \n3\n \n2026\n \n \n\n 2026 Gubernatorial General Election\n General Election\n \n\n Election Information Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nJun\n \n2\n \n2026\n \n \n\n 2026 Primary Election\n Primary Election\n \n\n Results by Precinct · Official Results\n Results Summary · Official Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n \n\n \nMar\n \n3\n \n2026\n \n \n\n Davenport/North Scott/Pleasant Valley PPEL/City of Walcott Vacancy Election 2026\n Special Election\n \n\n Official Summary Report · Official Results\n Unofficial Results\n Sample Ballot(s)\n \n \n \n \n\n\n\n\n\n\n \n\n News\n \n\n Absentee Ballot Stats Map\n \n September 28, 2026 \n\n\n\n\n 11 am Turnout Numbers for 3/3/26 Special Election\n\n\n\n 3-3-26 4 PM Turnout Numbers\n\n\nAll News\n \n \n\n \n FAQ\n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nWhat if I'm still waiting in line when the polls close?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nSo long as you are in line to vote at the time the polls close you will be allowed to vote.  \n\n \n\n \n \n\n \nQ.\n \n\nI lost my absentee ballot; can I just go vote on Election Day?\n \n\n \n \n\n \nA.\n \n\nYes. When you go to vote, a poll worker will verify with the auditor’s office that your absentee ballot has not been returned. If it is confirmed that the auditor’s office has not received a ballot from you then you will be given a new ballot to vote there. \n\n \n\n \n \nAll Frequently Asked Questions\n \n \n\n \n Scott County Voter Registration\n \n\n Updated October 1, 2026\n \n\n\n \nNo Party\n \n\n\n \n47,950\n \n\n \nDemocratic\n \n\n\n \n37,934\n \n\n \nRepublican\n \n\n\n \n37,306\n \n\n \nOther\n \n\n\n \n1,125\n \n\n \n \n \nTotal Registered Voters: 124,315\n \n\n Full Breakout\n Historical Data\n \n \n \n\n\n\n\nThis webpage was printed on October 17, 2026. For the most current election-related information, visit the Scott County, Iowa, Elections website at https://elections.scottcountyiowa.gov.\n\n\n \n\n Address\n\n 600 W. 4th St.\n \nDavenport, Iowa 52801\n\n Contact Us\n\n Accessibility\n\n Scott County Website\n \n \nOffice Hours\n\n Monday - Friday\n \n8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. \n \nPhone\n\n (563) 326-8631 \n \n\n \n\n \n \n\n\n\n\n \npowered by \n\n\n\n\n\n"
